# Land Rover Discovery 1 five-door, 1989-1998.
#
# The first Discovery: the three-box five-door on the Range Rover Classic
# floorpan, with the stepped rear side glass, the external spare and the
# utilitarian interior. The five-door is the volume body; the three-door is
# not separately represented.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_Rover_Discovery
#
# Dimensions 4.539 x 1.793 x 1.966 m, wheelbase 2.540 m.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is the side profile from the pack; the front and
# rear three-quarters show the lamps and tailgate. The notes state the angle.
#
# Colours: grade (b), factory-derived names from a Land Rover parts
# catalogue, with no built shares. Coniston Green, Beluga Black, Chawton
# White and Altai Silver are common on British roads. Weights 12, 10, 10, 8,
# total 40, provisional.
#
# Speed 160 km/h. Comfort 70/285, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 70: a tall,
# upright, utilitarian cabin. Classes 2,3.
# Dates are road presence: 1989 intro, retires staggered 2014-2017.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-1.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/land-rover-discovery-1.dae. References:
# citycars/references/land-rover-discovery-1/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the arch cladding is a flat ribbon rather than a moulded
# lip, the alpine roof windows are flat panels without surrounds, the roof bars
# are not modelled and the wheels are plain discs. At 128 px the tall boxy body,
# stepped roof and tailgate-mounted spare read as a Discovery 1.


obj=citycar
name=LandRoverDiscovery1(ConistonGreen)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1989
intro_month=10
retire_year=2017
retire_month=6
speed=160
class=2,3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=70
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=285

